{"rule": "Return this JSON object with the rule field unchanged and a new passage of about 250 words in the text field.", "text": "Neither of them breathed. The ticking came again, patient and exact, and Mira realized with a slow, cold wonder that it was matching the tremor of the arm, beat for beat, as though two clocks in two distant rooms had found each other across the dark. Tobias turned his head toward her, his face pale in the candlelight. \"It's keeping time,\" he said. \"Or we are keeping its.\" She wrote the words without deciding to, her pencil steadier now, the letters marching neatly along the line. Eleven fifty-four. External rhythm. Synchronous. Then she set the notebook down and crossed to the window. The glass was cold beneath her palm, and on the other side of it the ridge lay black against a sky crowded with more stars than she had ever seen there, clustered thickly above the notch where the old road ran. One of them was moving. It drifted down along the slope in small, deliberate steps, pausing between each, and with every pause the ticking sounded and the arm behind her shivered in reply. \"Tobias,\" she said, and did not know how to finish. He came to stand beside her. For a while they only watched, shoulder to shoulder, as the light descended toward the valley and the house and the two of them. The candle guttered, leaned, and went out. In the sudden dark the arm began to swing again, freely now, easily, as if whatever it had been waiting for had finally agreed to come."}
